WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.749 --> 00:00:15.649
Fly away!"

2
00:00:15.669 --> 00:00:17.030
the statue yelled.

3
00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:22.772
"Fast!" The statue's stone arm was heading for Swallow.

4
00:00:24.113 --> 00:00:27.794
Then—crack! The other arm broke off too!

5
00:00:29.755 --> 00:00:32.016
Swallow was too weak to even lift his head.

6
00:00:34.188 --> 00:00:37.071
Whoosh! The hawk suddenly swooped in.

7
00:00:38.412 --> 00:00:41.494
It grabbed Swallow with its claws and shot upward.

8
00:00:42.695 --> 00:00:44.877
The arms smashed onto the ground.

9
00:00:44.897 --> 00:00:49.101
"Leave Swallow alone!"

10
00:00:49.461 --> 00:00:50.462
the statue shouted.

11
00:00:50.482 --> 00:00:52.804
"Put him down!"

12
00:00:54.986 --> 00:00:58.769
But the hawk flew in close circles around the statue.

13
00:01:00.610 --> 00:01:02.312
He clutched Swallow tightly.

14
00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:06.962
"It's all for the best," Swallow said weakly.

15
00:01:06.982 --> 00:01:10.605
"I'm glad I helped you, Prince.

16
00:01:12.626 --> 00:01:15.588
I used to admire beautiful things with all my heart.

17
00:01:17.309 --> 00:01:20.851
But now I know it's better to fill my heart with love.

18
00:01:22.272 --> 00:01:23.933
Thank you for showing me that."

19
00:01:26.475 --> 00:01:30.458
Swallow's head drooped as the statue's belt crumbled to the ground.

20
00:01:33.580 --> 00:01:35.821
Kee-kee! The hawk let out a happy call.

21
00:01:35.841 --> 00:01:39.203
"You're so cruel!"

22
00:01:39.223 --> 00:01:40.603
the statue said.

23
00:01:40.623 --> 00:01:46.426
"I'm crumbling, and my dear friend is dying!"

24
00:01:49.627 --> 00:01:51.508
The hawk gripped Swallow tightly.

25
00:01:51.528 --> 00:01:56.910
"I'm happy because I've waited for this day a long time!"

26
00:02:02.864 --> 00:02:04.905
The statue made a wailing sound.

27
00:02:06.646 --> 00:02:12.990
Then—boom! It crumbled into a pile of stone and dust.

28
00:02:16.611 --> 00:02:18.212
The hawk waited for the air to clear.

29
00:02:19.533 --> 00:02:23.355
Then it gently placed Swallow in a spot of warm sunlight.

30
00:02:24.696 --> 00:02:28.078
The hawk flapped its wings and walked around Swallow.

31
00:02:30.679 --> 00:02:32.120
The sunlight started to shimmer.

32
00:02:35.784 --> 00:02:38.106
Swallow blinked at the bright light.

33
00:02:39.407 --> 00:02:40.828
His feathers warmed.

34
00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:47.053
Slowly he stood up and stretched his wings.

35
00:02:47.073 --> 00:02:52.076
"I'm not cold anymore," Swallow said.

36
00:02:52.097 --> 00:02:54.158
"And I'm not tired.

37
00:02:55.539 --> 00:02:56.740
How is this possible?"

38
00:02:58.862 --> 00:03:01.704
But then he saw the pile of stone and dust.

39
00:03:05.900 --> 00:03:07.461
"Prince!" he cried.

40
00:03:07.481 --> 00:03:09.662
"What happened to him?"

41
00:03:09.682 --> 00:03:14.043
"All will be well now," the hawk said.

42
00:03:14.063 --> 00:03:18.925
"But but Swallow could barely speak.

43
00:03:18.945 --> 00:03:21.387
"The statue is gone!"

44
00:03:24.108 --> 00:03:25.268
The hawk nodded.

45
00:03:25.288 --> 00:03:27.269
"Yes, he is.

46
00:03:28.249 --> 00:03:29.750
And it's all thanks to you!"

47
00:03:32.611 --> 00:03:34.352
Swallow felt his heart crack.

48
00:03:35.524 --> 00:03:37.726
"You mean I did this to him?"

49
00:03:37.746 --> 00:03:42.950
"No, you did not," the hawk said.

50
00:03:42.970 --> 00:03:45.051
"I did."

51
00:03:47.573 --> 00:03:51.396
The hawk flapped its wings once, twice, three times.

52
00:03:54.418 --> 00:03:56.840
Then light swirled into the air.

53
00:03:58.841 --> 00:04:02.144
Poof! The ruined statue disappeared.

54
00:04:04.856 --> 00:04:05.997
Swallow gasped.

55
00:04:07.158 --> 00:04:08.139
"What's happening?"

56
00:04:08.159 --> 00:04:14.244
"The spell is finally broken," the hawk said.

57
00:04:16.426 --> 00:04:18.728
Swallow was even more confused.

58
00:04:18.748 --> 00:04:20.989
"What spell?"

59
00:04:23.111 --> 00:04:24.773
The hawk dropped its head.

60
00:04:24.793 --> 00:04:28.956
"The one I never should have put on him."

61
00:04:28.976 --> 00:04:33.640
"Oh no," Swallow whispered.

62
00:04:34.988 --> 00:04:37.930
"Are you saying that my friend is gone forever?"

63
00:04:37.950 --> 00:04:45.036
"No." A boy stepped out from behind the rosebush.

64
00:04:45.056 --> 00:04:50.000
"Swallow! I am right here!"
